window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Can envy be tamed, or will it destroy everything?</p> <p>In the ninth volume of the Xane series, author Mark White delves into the complex and destructive emotion of envy. Xane finds herself at the center of a storm when Shari, a bandmate, reveals her deep-seated envy towards Xane. This revelation sets off a chain of events that forces Xane to confront the darker side of human emotions.</p> <p>As Xane navigates the tension within the band, she turns to the Analyst for guidance. Through introspective conversations, Xane learns that envy is often a reflection of the envier's own insecurities and perceived shortcomings. With this understanding, Xane strives to set emotional boundaries and protect her sense of self-worth.</p> <p>The narrative also explores the impact of envy on relationships, particularly between Shari and Russ. As the band prepares for a high-stakes New Year's Eve performance at the <i>haunted Davenport Theater</i>, they face eerie occurrences that test their resilience and unity. Despite the challenges, Xane and her bandmates deliver a memorable performance, ultimately growing closer and more resilient.</p> <p><i>Envy </i>is a powerful exploration of emotional intelligence, highlighting the complexities of envy and the importance of self-worth and empathy in overcoming negative emotions. Join Xane as she learns to navigate envy, set emotional boundaries, and find strength in her journey.</p>"; 
